          %h2#Idea Idea
          %p
            In
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/point-set+topology"} point-set topology
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/separation+axioms"} separation axioms
            that are traditionally considered on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+spaces"} topological spaces
            turn out (
            %a{:href => "#Gavrolovich14"}> Gavrilovich 2014
            ) to have an equivalent reformulation in terms of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lifting+properties"} lifting properties
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+topological+spaces"} finite topological spaces
            which reflects the “opposite property” or the “archetypical counterexample” to the given separation condition, in a sense (“
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+negation"}> Quillen negation
            ”).
          %p
            To see this, first notice/recall the following two basic examples of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lifting+properties"} lifting properties
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagrams"} diagrams
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/TopSp"} TopSp
          %p The property
          %ul
            %li
              %em>
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mover
                        %mo →
                        %mi f
                      %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \xrightarrow{f} Y
                is a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/surjective+function"} surjective function
              \.
          %p
            means equivalently that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            has the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+lifting+property"} right lifting property
            against the unique map from the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/empty+space"} empty space
            to the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/point+space"} point space
