          %h3#separated_by_closed_neighbourhoods Separated by closed neighbourhoods
          %p
            We say that a disjoint pair of subsets
            %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:APairOfDisjointSubsets"} (3)
            is
            %strong separated by neighbourhoods
            if the sets have
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/disjoint+subset"} disjoint
            closed
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/neighbourhoods"} neighbourhoods
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                  %mo ⊆
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U\subseteq V
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                  %mo ⊆
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V\subseteq G
            such that their closures
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bar U
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bar V
            do not intersect
          #eq:PairOfSeparatedClosedNeighbourhoods.maruku-equation
            %span.maruku-eq-number (8)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                  %mo ⊆
                  %mi V
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mtext and
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi V
                  %mo ⊆
                  %mi G
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mtext such that
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mover
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                  %mo ∩
                  %mover
                    %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo =
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ∅
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  U \subseteq V
                  \\;\text{and}\;
                  V \subseteq G
                  \\;\;\;\;\;\;
                  \\text{such that}
                  \\;\;\;\;\;\;
                  \\bar U \cap \bar V
                  \\;=\;
                  \\varnothing
          %p
            The separation condition
            %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:PairOfSeparatedClosedNeighbourhoods"} (8)
            on a pair of disjoint subsets means equivalently that their characteristic function
