          %p
            With this notation, we have the following dictionary between
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lifting+properties"} lifting properties
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/separation+axioms"} separation axioms
          %h3#KolmogorovSpaces
            Kolmogorov spaces (
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi T
                    %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T_0
            )
          %p
            A topological space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {X}
            is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/T0-space"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi T
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T_0
            (or
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kolmogorov+topological+space"} Kolmogorov
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {X}
            are
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#TopologicallyDisjoint"} topologically disjoint
          %p
            (It will be a common theme among the following separation axioms to have one version of an axiom that requires
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi T
                    %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T_0
            and one version that doesn’t.)
          %p
            This condition is equivalent to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lifting+property"} lifting property
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi x
                  %mo ↔
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi x
                  %mo =
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mi ⧄
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\big(
                  \\{x\leftrightarrow y\} \longrightarrow  \{x=y\}
                  \\big)
                  \\;\;\,&amp;solb;\,\;\;
                  \\big(
                  {X} \longrightarrow  \{*\}
                  \\big)
          %p hence:
