          %h3#SymmetricSpaces
            Symmetric spaces (
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi R
                    %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R_0
            )
          %p
            A topological space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {X}
            is an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/R0-space"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi R
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R_0
              \-space
            (also:
            = succeed ")," do
              %em symmetric space
            %a{:href => "#TopologicallyDisjoint"} topologically distinguishable
            points in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            are
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#TopologicallySeparated"} topologically separated
          %p
            This condition is equivalent to the following
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lifting+property"} lifting property
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi x
                  %mo ↘
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi x
                  %mo ↔
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mi ⧄
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\big(
                  \\{x{\searrow}y\} \longrightarrow  \{x\leftrightarrow y\}
                  \\big)
                  \\;\;\;\,&amp;solb;\,\;\;\;
                  \\big(
                  {X} \longrightarrow  \{*\}
                  \\big)
                  \\,.
          %h3#LiftingPropertyCorrespondingtoT1
            Accessible spaces (
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi T
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T_1
            )
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/T1-space"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi T
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T_1
            (or
            %em accessible
            or
            = succeed ")" do
              %em Fréchet
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            are separated, i.e.
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi x
                  %mo ↘
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi x
                  %mo =
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mi ⧄
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi X
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\{x{\searrow}y\} \longrightarrow  \{x=y\}
                  \\;\;\;\,&amp;solb;\,\;\;\;
                  {X} \longrightarrow  \{*\}
          %p
            Thus,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is T1 if and only if it is both T0 and R0: indeed, a morphism lifts wrt the composition
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi x
                  %mo ↘
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi x
                  %mo ↔
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi x
                  %mo =
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{x{\searrow}y\} \longrightarrow  \{x\leftrightarrow y\} \longrightarrow  \{x=y\}
            iff it lifts wrt either one of the two morphisms. (Although you may say such things as “T1 space”, “Frechet topology”, and “Suppose that the topological space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is Frechet”, avoid saying “Frechet space” in this context, since there is another entirely different notion of Frechet space in functional analysis.)
