          %h3#reregular_spaces_
            Reregular spaces (
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi R
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R_1
            )
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is R1, or preregular, if any two topologically distinguishable points in X are separated by neighbourhoods. Every R1 space is also R0.
          %h3#weakly_hausdorff_spaces Weakly Hausdorff spaces
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weakly+Hausdorff+topological+space"} weakly Hausdorff
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+Hausdorff+space"} compact Hausdorff space
            into
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is closed. All weak Hausdorff spaces are T1, and all Hausdorff spaces are weak Hausdorff.
          %h3#hausdorff_spaces_
            Hausdorff spaces (
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi T
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T_2
            )
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hausdorff+space"} Hausdorff
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            are separated by neighbourhoods, i.e.
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %mo ↪
                  %munder
                    %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mi ⧄
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi x
                  %mo ↘
                  %munder
                    %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %mo ↙
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi x
                  %mo =
                  %mi X
