          %p
            Indeed, in the interesting case that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            maps to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            by the top horizontal arrow, the separating neighbourhoods would be the preimage under the diagonal arrow of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %menclose{:notation => "box"}
                    %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{\boxed{x}\}
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mover
                      %mrow
                      %menclose{:notation => "box"}
                        %mi U
                    %mo ↘
                    %munder
                      %mrow
                      %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{\overset{\boxed{U}}{}\searrow\underset{F}{}\}
          %p
            In fact, in a regular space, any such
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {x}
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {F}
            will also be separated by closed neighbourhoods obtained by “applying” the lifting property again to
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mover
                      %mrow
                      %menclose{:notation => "box"}
                        %mi x
                    %mo ↘
                    %munder
                      %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                        %mo =
                        %mi U
                        %mo =
                        %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{\overset{\boxed{x}}{}\searrow\underset{X=U=F}{}\}
          %h3#regular_hausdorff_space_
            Regular Hausdorff space (
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi T
                    %mn 3
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T_3
            )
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regular+Hausdorff+space"} regular Hausdorff space
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                    %mn 2
                    %mfrac
                      %mn 1
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T2\frac{1}{2}
          %h3#completely_regular_spaces Completely regular spaces
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is completely regular if, given any point
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {x}
            and closed set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            such that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {x}
            does not belong to
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mi X
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mi ⧄
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %msub
                    %mo ∨
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ↔
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mover
                    %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi e
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mn 0
                          %mo ,
                          %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo ↘
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\{x\} \longrightarrow  {X}
                  \\;\;\;\,&amp;solb;\,\;\;\;
                  [0,1] \vee_{\{1\}} {\{1\leftrightarrow F\}}
                  \\longrightarrow  \{ \overset{e_{[0,1]}}{}  \searrow F\}
          %p
            Here in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %msub
                    %mo ∨
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ↔
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [0,1] \vee_{\{1\}} {\{1\leftrightarrow F\}}
            the points
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
            are topologically indistinguishable,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [0,1]
            goes to
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            goes to
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
          %p Every completely regular space is also regular.
          %h3#tychonoff_spaces_
            Tychonoff spaces (
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi T
                    %mrow
                      %mn 3
                      %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                        %mfrac
                          %mn 1
                          %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T_{3 \tfrac{1}{2}}
            )
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tychonoff+space"} Tychonoff
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mfrac
                      %mn 1
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{1}{2}
          %h3#normal_spaces Normal spaces
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/normal+topological+space"} normal
            if any two disjoint closed subsets of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            are separated by neighbourhoods, i.e.
